{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1083493-just-do-it-the-high-tech-way","id":1083493,"title":"Just do it the high-tech way","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-25T09:21:36-07:00","id":1083493,"title":"Just do it the high-tech way","content":"So I have been thinking about magick in relation to my work. I work at a bank, and when people come in asking for things like cash, paper statements, checks, etc, I always wonder what's keeping them from doing things the more high-tech way. This lead naturally (of course) to me thinking about the Syndicate, and then to how the Technocracy works.<br /> So I know that per canon most Technocrats don't see what they do as &quot;magic&quot; it's Enlightened Science, which is cool on it's own. But, what if the Technocracy viewed themselves as just the advanced modern magic users? Basically, why are you using dirt and trees and crystals when you can use computers and guns and stuff?<br /> I know this changes a lot, making the Technocracy maybe a little kinder and gentler, and I know a lot of people won't like that. And I know this could potentially not work with the idea of consensual reality, which has always been confusing and hard to do right for me anyways. I guess this could be a more recent development. This doesn't mean that the Pogrom had to go away, obviously, particularly since Technocrats view the Traditions as unstable and dangerous to everyone magic users.<br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T09:42:52-07:00","id":1083510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Basically, why are you using dirt and trees and crystals when you can use computers and guns and stuff? </div> </div> </div>Like, say, what Virtual Adepts do? :P<br /> <br /> You will have to change not only the Technocracy, but also the Traditions to do what you intend.<br /> <br /> Turning the Traditions into a bunch of primitivists that don't accept the modernization of magick it's arguably a huger (and worse, to my point of view) change than to say that the Technocracy file and rank understands the methapysics of magick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T10:22:17-07:00","id":1083532,"title":"","content":"It's definitely an interesting concept for a game variation. I think that this variation would require some serious reworking of the organizational history. Especially with regards to the Sons of Ether and the Virtual Adepts. They would likely need very different roles and reasons for leaving the Technocracy, assuming they leave at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T10:34:34-07:00","id":1083538,"title":"","content":"You're assuming that modern is better inherently, or that it's true in the world of darkness, which isn't true for Magick. That is true for technological practicioners. That is true for our world (since the technocracy is a super conspiracy to explain our modernization!)<br /> <br /> &quot;Better&quot; is what fits your focus. Your modern verbena witch-detective obviously has a computer and ocasionally finds partners for holy communion on Tinder. She still bleeds for power and draws from her connection to the earth to see what the small animals of the neighborhood have seen recently. She starves naked under the moonlight for three days because that's how you build up for a prophecy.<br /> Your urban akashic sees the endless cacophony as just another hurdle to centering and emptying his mind, which will make him stronger. Modern medicine gives an useful framework for him to apply his chi channeling techniques where applicable. He'll still order his preferred incense from amazon since that nice peddler that smells faintly of rotten clove stopped coming to your neighborhood.<br /> <br /> Because that's how it works. Modernization of magickal practices must occur under their limitations. (just like how IRL modernization of productivity involves automation, since bettering people reached a viability cap)<br /> Who's to say the current grimoires on Simplified Enochian don't have more extensive, specific and effective entries for establishing dominance over dream-entities? Your complete facebook profile is definitely a level 4 simpathetic connection instead of 5.<br /> <br /> <br /> As the setting is drawn by standard most mages embrace technology. It just happens to be separate from how they do magic. For a mystic they're handy tools at best and deviations from the Way Things Should Be at worst.<br /> <br /> <br /> That said, you definitely have space to widen that gap between mysticism and the modern world. That is the primary consequence of the technocratic struggle and is to the detriment of the traditions. It's just that I agree with Aleph and feel that making the tech-haters traditionalists common instead of minoritary is kinda meh. The technocratic zeitgeist admitting what they do is definitely as impossible as what the mystics do is alright, and brings lots of uncomfortable questions to the upper echelons. They also very definitely succeeded at mundanizing many things they would call impossible a few decades before though, so &quot;we do magic&quot; is probably going to be as rare and scoffed as it is by default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 04-25-2017, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T14:14:58-07:00","id":1083686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1083493-just-do-it-the-high-tech-way?p=1083510#post1083510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like, say, what Virtual Adepts do? :P<br /> <br /> You will have to change not only the Technocracy, but also the Traditions to do what you intend.<br /> <br /> Turning the Traditions into a bunch of primitivists that don't accept the modernization of magick it's arguably a huger (and worse, to my point of view) change than to say that the Technocracy file and rank understands the methapysics of magick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except.... that's exactly what they are. Sure, they develop their own forms and do indeed march forward into the future rather than stagnating entirely.... but each of the traditions is essentially someone taking Magic As It Was, and enshrining it as the holy one way.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy's Enlightened Science on the other hand. Has changed drastically over the years in response to the shifting goals of the union itself. At one point, magical gems that allowed communication were allowed. And a few of them are even grandfathered in for particularly old members of Control since they don't see the proles much anyway.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, while the Hermetics will innovate within their system. You would never expect to see them tear their system down to the basics and restart from scratch the way the Union does. Meaning they'll always be shackled to that outdated means of using magic. To abandon Enochian, their knowledge of the angels and demons and the binding thereof and all other trappings of their art in order to remake it.<br /> <br /> The balance to this of course, is the Traditions tendency to allow it's members to awaken past Arete 6 and start surrendering their paradigm and realizing it's all will etc etc.<br /> <br /> The Union Starts off at that point, but obfuscates it. Meaning it's more versatile on a lower level than the Traditions. While sacrificing the individual power of it's members.<br /> <br /> The traditions are much like a group of people who got off the train at some point and stuck with windows 95. They don't exactly stagnate. But they are marked by their insistence on using this old platform to advance with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T17:23:23-07:00","id":1083759,"title":"","content":"That's not really true in the updated Tradition books. The Trads mix in technocratic stuff with their mystical symbols and such. I think that WW realized that they had made the Traditions less free than the supposedly oppressive Technocrats. So they made an effort in later material to make it clear that the Traditions were indeed about freedom and tolerance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T18:27:29-07:00","id":1083774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1083493-just-do-it-the-high-tech-way?p=1083759#post1083759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not really true in the updated Tradition books. The Trads mix in technocratic stuff with their mystical symbols and such. I think that WW realized that they had made the Traditions less free than the supposedly oppressive Technocrats. So they made an effort in later material to make it clear that the Traditions were indeed about freedom and tolerance.</div> </div> </div> </div>This development also worked to add a tactic to the Traditions' arsenal: co-opting the Technocracy's tools, so as to beat the Union at its own game. Pull the rug right out from under them, to quote M20's section on the Taftani.<br /> <br /> See, the conflict between Traditions and Technocracy never really was about technology, tools, and techniques. It was about ideology and world view. By claiming the tools of the Technocracy as their own, Tradition technomancers proved that their Paradigms were not invalid in the modern era. Weaving a spell into an email doesn't need to discredit the world view from which that spell was generated; Hermetic House Thig knows that the astrological signs are just as powerful now as they were 500 years ago. The Chorister Alexandrian Society sees no conflict between an ordered universe full of physical laws, and an almighty God who created it (and can break those laws as He sees fit).<br /> <br /> For the Technocracy, the tools, technologies, and techniques themselves are all that matter. Meaning anything outside them is impossible. Or at least that's what they want everyone (including their own lower ranks) to think, as it keeps magick under their control. When the Traditions adopt modern technology to their own Paradigms, it's an act that refutes the Union's very premise.<br /> <br /> If the common people can have magic and miracles, <i>in addition to machines</i>, why should the world need a Technocracy at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T08:42:12-07:00","id":1083988,"title":"","content":"Indeed, the Traditions cannot be a bunch of primitivists that don't accept the modernization of magick because they allow for all kind of practices, both old and new, inside their structure. This was true even before Revised (with the addition of VA and Etherites), but was increased a thousandfold in Revised, as per the two previous comments show.<br /> <br /> To change this would imply that the Virtual Adepts would have to go away, all the technomancer camps (and every Tradition have them) would cease to exist or join the Union, and the Etherites would have to surrender all technology but the strictly deprecated, and even then they would be shuned for not being primitive enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T09:14:46-07:00","id":1084002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1083493-just-do-it-the-high-tech-way?p=1083686#post1083686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Meanwhile, while the Hermetics will innovate within their system. You would never expect to see them tear their system down to the basics and restart from scratch the way the Union does. Meaning they'll always be shackled to that outdated means of using magic. To abandon Enochian, their knowledge of the angels and demons and the binding thereof and all other trappings of their art in order to remake it.<br /> <br /> The traditions are much like a group of people who got off the train at some point and stuck with windows 95. They don't exactly stagnate. But they are marked by their insistence on using this old platform to advance with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that that's not true. The Hermetics are constantly inovating in substantial ways that can be just as fundamental as anything the Union does. The history of coming up with new methodologies and discarding old ones seems like it's pretty much the same. Witness the Houses that have come and gone vs. the Conventions that have come and gone. Witness the internal redefinition of what a House does and how it works vs. the same with the Conventions. A power-hungry nigh-authoritarian modern Tytalus doesn't have a lot in common with a boisterous boundary breaker Tytalus from back in the day. The N.W.O is definitely a different take on the idea of &quot;ideology magic&quot; than the Ivory Tower. Both sets of groups are doing the same thing as the predecessors in slightly different ways for what can be significantly different reasons.<br /> <br /> As far as this rigid continuity of the Hermetics.... The case might be made that Hermetics made an even bigger shift in fundamental ideology than the remanant of the Order of Reason made in the shift to the Technocratic Union. The DA Hermetics up through to the Renaissance weren't doing anything thing with binding angels and demons. Both were pretty much forbidden for different reasons. There was a huge shift in how Hermetics thought about magic that was completed by the Renaissance. And another when the whole Tradtion went Theosophist in the 19th Century. All this &quot;MY WILL&quot; and obsession with True Names and Enochian are changes from the Order as founded by Bonisagus and Trianoma back in the Dark Ages.<br /> <br /> In fact, unlike the Union, the Hermetics actually have Ex Misc., an explicit incubator House for coming up with new ideas on how to implement magic (Thig, Fortunae, etc.). Which also serves as a place to shelve old ideologies for their potential future usefulness. The Hermetics, unlike the Union, are great synthesizers, particularly if you buy into a current order that has taken up the Ngoma and the Wu Lung.<br /> <br /> And, since pretty much all of the Traditions are actually versions of the idea of &quot;including many different ideas under the same umbrella&quot;, similar situations can be found. The Celestial Chorus certainly has become VERY ecumenical. The Euthanatos are pretty much a grab bag of different magical praxes with the loosest of common ground.<br /> <br /> And they make that WORK. Which requires innovative thought all over the place. And they keep adding in new things. If you were correct with your Windows95, then the Verbena would be druids and witches. No way for modern versions of paganism to intrude. Chakravanti Euthanatos wouldn't be able to use sniper rifles to do magic. It'd be all &quot;kukri and kris and strangling cords&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 05-04-2017, 08:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T09:32:43-07:00","id":1084009,"title":"","content":"Delete please","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 04-26-2017, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T10:01:59-07:00","id":1084033,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3598_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3598\" data-vbnamecard=\"3598\">CajunKhan</a> :That's most likely to be the case. But are you commenting in the right thread?, I think not. Surely you missed it by an inch, I hate when that happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T17:44:34-07:00","id":1084217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1083493-just-do-it-the-high-tech-way?p=1083774#post1083774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This development also worked to add a tactic to the Traditions' arsenal: co-opting the Technocracy's tools, so as to beat the Union at its own game. Pull the rug right out from under them, to quote M20's section on the Taftani.<br /> <br /> See, the conflict between Traditions and Technocracy never really was about technology, tools, and techniques. It was about ideology and world view. By claiming the tools of the Technocracy as their own, Tradition technomancers proved that their Paradigms were not invalid in the modern era. Weaving a spell into an email doesn't need to discredit the world view from which that spell was generated; Hermetic House Thig knows that the astrological signs are just as powerful now as they were 500 years ago. The Chorister Alexandrian Society sees no conflict between an ordered universe full of physical laws, and an almighty God who created it (and can break those laws as He sees fit).<br /> <br /> For the Technocracy, the tools, technologies, and techniques themselves are all that matter. Meaning anything outside them is impossible. Or at least that's what they want everyone (including their own lower ranks) to think, as it keeps magick under their control. When the Traditions adopt modern technology to their own Paradigms, it's an act that refutes the Union's very premise.<br /> <br /> If the common people can have magic and miracles, <i>in addition to machines</i>, why should the world need a Technocracy at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>But.... does it refute the unions premise? It really isn't. Modern Technomancers are a cargo cult at best. They ape the actions and trappings of technology without understanding the science, both enlightened and otherwise behind it. By claiming the Technocracy's tools, they have added their assenting voice to the consensus. the Consensus that says &quot;The Technocrats view of the world is correct.&quot; And the Technocrats view of the world <i>does not have a place for their magic. </i>It's not an obvious problem. But it is a problem, and the defining reason behind the Technocracy having won the Ascension War. Even the Traditions are contaminated with Technocratic ideas.<br /> <br /> Them 'weaving a spell into an email' doesn't discredit the world view from which that spell was generated. This is true. However it does CREDIT the world view from which the system to send that Email is created. And that worldview holds that the world is made up of consistent orderly physical laws with no exceptions. Physical laws that can be exploited to produce effects. There are no spirits. No almighty God. No mysticism. Just simple rules.<br /> <br /> By using this, they feel they have claimed something. And in Mage that does mean something. But it doesn't mean as much as they hope. Nor does it mean what they think it means.<br /> <br /> What are the Technocrats actual beliefs? Their ideological core? The thing that EVERY member of the Union knows? it's not the tech. It's not the Techniques. It's not even the science. All that's just tools.<br /> <br /> What they know is the Precepts of Damian. And if you read them there is actually very little to define the surface trappings of what they intend to build. No. What they're about is blocking out the Umbra, Defining the world and everything in it, destroying anything that cannot be defined, and uniting the masses of humanity under their banner so that all mankind might benefit when unity, and thus utopia and ascension is achieved.<br /> <br /> THIS is the belief that pushes the Technocracy forward. Whether it's the front line agent who's 'magic' takes the form of 'advanced combat training' the progenitor who's slinging around psychic powers and bio-engineered horrors, or the iterator who's building a plasma cannon the size of a city block. THIS is the belief that they all hold.<br /> <br /> Everything else is just a means to an end.<br /> <br /> The Traditions have taken their means. And forged that into their ends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T19:50:12-07:00","id":1084269,"title":"","content":"Yes, but in doing so they have proven that they don't need to exclude any Paradigm. In doing so they rewrite the technocratic world-view because they add things into the definitions that the Technocracy uses. Traditionalists use the means of the Technocracy to unblock the Umbra, to redefine the workings of the world (Etherites are especialy adept at this, with their way of twisting science, and then publishing it) and everything in it, to unify all forms of magick merging technology with the practices that said technology was developed to destroy. <i>And it works</i> , there are places where people doesn't believe that the technology can't coexist with local magic (you just need to dig a little to find out)<br /> <br /> The freedom that the Traditions wish to archieve would be impossible if they refuse to accept the means of the Technocracy into their ends. If they resisted that, then they would be no different from the Technos, they would be deffining a world by excluding a certain number of Practices. The Traditions cannot win if they can't twist the Practices that the Technocracy developed into something that can work with older Practices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-26-2017, 10:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T20:31:50-07:00","id":1084293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1083493-just-do-it-the-high-tech-way?p=1084269#post1084269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but in doing so they have proven that they don't need to exclude any Paradigm. In doing so they rewrite the technocratic world-view because they add things into the definitions that the Technocracy uses. Traditionalists use the means of the Technocracy to unblock the Umbra, to redefine the workings of the world (Etherites are especialy adept at this, with their way of twisting science, and then publishing it) and everything in it, to unify all forms of magick merging technology with the practices that said technology was developed to destroy. <i>And it works</i> , there are places where people doesn't believe that the technology can't coexist with local magic (you just need to dig a little to find out)<br /> <br /> The freedom that the Traditions wish to archieve would be impossible if they refuse to accept the means of the Technocracy into their ends. If they resisted that, then they would be no different from the Technos, they would be deffining a world by excluding a certain number of Practices. The Traditions cannot win if they can't twist the Practices that the Technocracy developed into something that can work with older Practices.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except it doesn't work, because as I said. The 'technology' is the surface trappings of the Technocratic practice. Everything that presently exists. That the Technocracy has. Is scheduled to be removed. It's a stepping stone. Not an end point.<br /> <br /> The Technocracies practice is essentially &quot;Unite the people with a single vision. Then make that vision a reality by communal effort. Guided by expert supervision.&quot; That is the one common denominator amongst every technocratic paradigm. And that is the one thing the Traditions don't, and can't adapt without losing who they are.<br /> <br /> They can't enforce a single worldview while arguing for multiple worldviews.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T07:57:34-07:00","id":1084483,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except it doesn't work, because as I said. The 'technology' is the surface trappings of the Technocratic practice. Everything that presently exists. That the Technocracy has. Is scheduled to be removed. It's a stepping stone. Not an end point.<br /> <br /> The Technocracies practice is essentially &quot;Unite the people with a single vision. Then make that vision a reality by communal effort. Guided by expert supervision.&quot; That is the one common denominator amongst every technocratic paradigm. And that is the one thing the Traditions don't, and can't adapt without losing who they are.<br /> <br /> They can't enforce a single worldview while arguing for multiple worldviews.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except it DOES work, because the 'technology' it's the surface trapping of technomancer focus. When everything disappear they will move along and invent a new rune for whatever the next big thing is.<br /> <br /> While a technomancer can grab the latest invention and scratch a rune at it, the Technocrat has to use the invention the way it was intended to be used, and has to work hard for years to create and popularize the next big thing. And there's nothing they can do to prevent the shaman from invoking the spirit of the next big thing and quickly advance magick both in his eyes and in the eyes of his people.<br /> <br /> In fact, the traditions ALSO push for the advancement of foci. Like the Etherites and their push of quantum physics that led to a lot of innovations in computer science. Or how Hermetics advanced magick to a point where it's totally different from what they did before.<br /> <br /> Traditionalists haven't a practice, what they have it's a meta-paradigm that posits that everything works. This isn't the same as arguing for multiple worldviews. In fact, they don't argue for &quot;multiple worldviews&quot;, but for a single a worldview that's dynamic, that can assimilate other worldviews (and this is why the Disparates don't like them. The Disparates are the ones that trully argue for a multiple worldview).<br /> <br /> To archieve this they don't need to include what you wrongly call the &quot;technocratical practice&quot; (it isn't a practice but a meta-paradigm, practice it's what you do, paradigm it's the conceptual trapping that explains why are you using a concrete practice at a given moment) , they just need to be able to include every new practice the Technocracy produces as part of their worldview faster than the Technocracy can produce them. They don't need to respect the unionist message of the Technocracy, they want to defeat that message, and they do so proving that any new practice the Technocracy endorses can be adapted to acomodate their beliefs.<br /> <br /> In doing so witches keep making business and getting new believers that will link the power of whatever the Technocrats do with runes, spirits or whatever uncontroled paradigm they need-and <i>the Technocracy doesn't want this, because it undermines the principles they're working to build</i>. Because if some people believes that you need the blessing of spirits to be a good hacker, and other believes that you need the power of the runes, then &quot;computation&quot; it's no longer universal, no longer objective...then the Technocracy may replace computation with something else, but soon that something else will be related to the spirits too, and to runes, etc. In the end, if Technocracy want's Unity, they will have no other choice but to accept that everything can work within their single vision...and that's the single worldview of the Traditions","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-27-2017, 11:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T10:31:56-07:00","id":1084552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1083493-just-do-it-the-high-tech-way?p=1084483#post1084483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While a technomancer can grab the latest invention and scratch a rune at it, the Technocrat has to use the invention the way it was intended to be used, and has to work hard for years to create and popularize the next big thing. And there's nothing they can do to prevent the shaman from invoking the spirit of the next big thing and quickly advance magick both in his eyes and in the eyes of his people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, a Technocrat has to work hard for years to create AND popularize the next big thing, but really, they don't need to popularize something to be able to do it. One is praxis. The other is adherence to the Time Table. Technocrats are making up next big things all the time in seconds flat. Note that using their magic does not demand &quot;Extra Time: Months&quot; and/or &quot;R&amp;D lab with appropriate materials required&quot;. They can jury-rig thing X to have it do function y, even it's designed to do function x in the field. Even in the space of several seconds if the need it pressing.<br /> <br /> Which means they really don't do things very different from other mages at all. In terms of Focus as defined as a game concept, the Union's insistence on the blinders on what they are doing fundamentally are really just rank sophistry. And counter-productive at that, because the fact that those other guys who do magic are obviously doing exactly the same things functionally means that Conditioning and Reconditioning for ANY operatives that come into contact with other ways of doing things is going to be frequent and brutal.<br /> <br /> And there are so many EASIER ways to explain the whole situation that work much, much better. &quot;We do this stuff (change the nature of reality) the SAFE way. That's what technology is. They are playing fast and loose with the rules of reality and it's DANGEROUS. That's why they need to be stopped. For the good of reality as whole. For the good of humanity. For their own good.&quot;<br /> <br /> And that's just ONE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 04-27-2017, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T14:53:35-07:00","id":1084710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1083493-just-do-it-the-high-tech-way?p=1084483#post1084483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except it DOES work, because the 'technology' it's the surface trapping of technomancer focus. When everything disappear they will move along and invent a new rune for whatever the next big thing is.<br /> <br /> While a technomancer can grab the latest invention and scratch a rune at it, the Technocrat has to use the invention the way it was intended to be used, and has to work hard for years to create and popularize the next big thing. And there's nothing they can do to prevent the shaman from invoking the spirit of the next big thing and quickly advance magick both in his eyes and in the eyes of his people.<br /> <br /> In fact, the traditions ALSO push for the advancement of foci. Like the Etherites and their push of quantum physics that led to a lot of innovations in computer science. Or how Hermetics advanced magick to a point where it's totally different from what they did before.<br /> <br /> Traditionalists haven't a practice, what they have it's a meta-paradigm that posits that everything works. This isn't the same as arguing for multiple worldviews. In fact, they don't argue for &quot;multiple worldviews&quot;, but for a single a worldview that's dynamic, that can assimilate other worldviews (and this is why the Disparates don't like them. The Disparates are the ones that trully argue for a multiple worldview).<br /> <br /> To archieve this they don't need to include what you wrongly call the &quot;technocratical practice&quot; (it isn't a practice but a meta-paradigm, practice it's what you do, paradigm it's the conceptual trapping that explains why are you using a concrete practice at a given moment) , they just need to be able to include every new practice the Technocracy produces as part of their worldview faster than the Technocracy can produce them. They don't need to respect the unionist message of the Technocracy, they want to defeat that message, and they do so proving that any new practice the Technocracy endorses can be adapted to acomodate their beliefs.<br /> <br /> In doing so witches keep making business and getting new believers that will link the power of whatever the Technocrats do with runes, spirits or whatever uncontroled paradigm they need-and <i>the Technocracy doesn't want this, because it undermines the principles they're working to build</i>. Because if some people believes that you need the blessing of spirits to be a good hacker, and other believes that you need the power of the runes, then &quot;computation&quot; it's no longer universal, no longer objective...then the Technocracy may replace computation with something else, but soon that something else will be related to the spirits too, and to runes, etc. In the end, if Technocracy want's Unity, they will have no other choice but to accept that everything can work within their single vision...and that's the single worldview of the Traditions</div> </div> </div> </div>You're still not getting it.<br /> <br /> The Union can invent things just as fast as the Traditions can. They in fact do. The reason why the traditions LOST the ascension war, is that they can't get their methods to work for everyone. Yes, for the individuals amongst the traditions. Everything works.<br /> <br /> These individuals are reality warpers. They don't count. The average man on the street CAN'T scratch a rune into a computer and have it work.* It just doesn't work that way. Think of it like this.<br /> <br /> The Technocrats are building. Piece by Piece. A world. the world is undefined and they are going through, from smallest part to largest and defining it. The traditions attempt to 'undefine' it again. Make it pliable again. But that's a lot harder than defining it in the first place. Particularly as they don't have a particularly strong grasp on how the Technocracy achieved their goals to start with.<br /> <br /> When the Traditions come up with some mystical way to use technology. What they're doing isn't redefining reality. Or rather it is. But they're affecting a surface trapping. They're changing one small chunk of the code and ignoring the vast sea around them. All it will do for anyone else is just cause errors. Break things. And that is the problem. If EVERYTHING is possible. Nothing is possible. If raising your arm is just as likely to light you on fire as not. Humanity can't survive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T15:04:57-07:00","id":1084716,"title":"","content":"I know this might sound like a dumb question but what exactly is being argued as working or not working?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T15:17:39-07:00","id":1084722,"title":"","content":"It's very simple, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12480_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12480\" data-vbnamecard=\"12480\">Spacecat</a>.<br /> <br /> When <i>you </i>got a haircut, you just changed the way you looked.<br /> <br /> When <i>I </i>got a haircut, I <i>reinvented </i>myself.<br /> <br /> These are, obviously, completely different, which is why you lost the Ascension war.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T15:21:19-07:00","id":1084724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1083493-just-do-it-the-high-tech-way?p=1084716#post1084716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know this might sound like a dumb question but what exactly is being argued as working or not working?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's hard to say, because the books themselves are deeply contradictory about it. Sometimes it seems like the White Wolfverse is purely metaphysically idealistic. Other suppliments imply that the Technocracy viewpoint is at least partially correct, and the Traditions are arguing about the margins. I think the problems comes in because (1)in the real world the Technocratic viewpoint IS correct, purely and absolutely, so it becomes difficult to detail the White-Wolfverse without either acknowleding that, or else making the WWverse nothing like the real world, when it's supposed to be a grim and gritty place that is still mostly the real world. And (2)for balance reasons they don't want the characters going completely nuts with the reality warping even in times or places where there should be no consensus.<br /> <br /> In short, there are plot holes inherent in the very core concept of Mage that make certain discussions unanswerable or messy at best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T15:21:31-07:00","id":1084725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1083493-just-do-it-the-high-tech-way?p=1084716#post1084716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know this might sound like a dumb question but what exactly is being argued as working or not working?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nothing at this point. Right now it's devolved into the classic technocrat vs tradition arguement. Notice the &quot;this is why X has already won forever&quot; and &quot;X is why Y will win in the end&quot; arguments that traditions and techies in a parallel universe would probably have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T15:24:40-07:00","id":1084729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1083493-just-do-it-the-high-tech-way?p=1084722#post1084722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's very simple, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12480_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12480\" data-vbnamecard=\"12480\">Spacecat</a>.<br /> <br /> When <i>you </i>got a haircut, you just changed the way you looked.<br /> <br /> When <i>I </i>got a haircut, I <i>reinvented </i>myself.<br /> <br /> These are, obviously, completely different, which is why you lost the Ascension war.</div> </div> </div> </div>Close but not quite.<br /> <br /> When I build an elaborate system of rules called 'physics' and these rules interact with one another in such a way as to cause 'computers' to work. It's very very different from you taking a lump of plastic. Carving runes into it and saying &quot;THE SPIRITS WILL THIS 'COMPUTER' TO BE THE BEST COMPUTER EVER.&quot; and then using reality warping to make it work.<br /> <br /> Enlightened science works by building the underlying ruleset. It's NOT just 'spells with a different name and motif.' Though that's part of it. This is why Atom Bombs were built by sleepers. Using the rules the Technocrats invented in a way the Technocrats themselves did not anticipate.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T15:36:56-07:00","id":1084735,"title":"","content":"I, of course, do not think that is a credible argument, which is why I chose to make light of it.<br /> <br /> In what secret tome, hidden from the eyes of the uninitiated, might a lowly seeker such as myself be revealed unto the True Doctrine of Mage: The Ascension?<br /> <br /> I wallow in horrible ignorance, with only the damnable heretic lies of the Books of Madness and Shadows to comfort me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T16:13:21-07:00","id":1084749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1083493-just-do-it-the-high-tech-way?p=1084735#post1084735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I, of course, do not think that is a credible argument, which is why I chose to make light of it.<br /> <br /> In what secret tome, hidden from the eyes of the uninitiated, might a lowly seeker such as myself be revealed unto the True Doctrine of Mage: The Ascension?<br /> <br /> I wallow in horrible ignorance, with only the damnable heretic lies of the Books of Madness and Shadows to comfort me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why. For twelve installments of 9.99 Primal Energy Credits per month, you too could be initiated into the true secrets of why the Technocracy is the best and most amazing faction ever! Or alternatively you could simply tune in to my daily or weekly fanboying and pick it up peicemeal.<br /> <br /> Also. Because I forgot to put it in post 17....<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">*Ironically enough. I actually DO carve symbols into the plastic shell of my laptops in order to bless them with good luck. Because IRL I'm a superstitious neo-pagan. The Irony abounds.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T16:28:59-07:00","id":1084752,"title":"","content":"I say then that the Technocracy will never truly win... because that won't make for a very fun game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T17:20:50-07:00","id":1084772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1083493-just-do-it-the-high-tech-way?p=1084752#post1084752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I say then that the Technocracy will never truly win... because that won't make for a very fun game.</div> </div> </div> </div>And so you grasp the wizened secrets of narrative causality. Neither side can ever truly win. Because that would mean the game is over and there'd be less toys to play with. : P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T10:03:41-07:00","id":1085064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Enlightened science works by building the underlying ruleset. It's NOT just 'spells with a different name and motif.' Though that's part of it. This is why Atom Bombs were built by sleepers. Using the rules the Technocrats invented in a way the Technocrats themselves did not anticipate.</div> </div> </div> </div>As has been said by other people in this thread, no book states that what enlightened science it's fundamentally different from magick in any way, the contrary has been stated multiple times. What the Traditions do it's no different that what the Technocrats do, the apparent difference of normal people being able to use technology it's just because they're currently winning the Ascencion War (or, rather, that's what BOTH factions believe). It doesn't prove that they can't loose nor that allowing technomagick isn't an important victory for the Traditions (a vicrory archieved against the Traditions themselves).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When the Traditions come up with some mystical way to use technology. What they're doing isn't redefining reality. Or rather it is. But they're affecting a surface trapping. They're changing one small chunk of the code and ignoring the vast sea around them. All it will do for anyone else is just cause errors. Break things. And that is the problem. If EVERYTHING is possible. Nothing is possible. If raising your arm is just as likely to light you on fire as not. Humanity can't survive. </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;If raising your arm is just as likely to light you on fire as not. &quot; it's not a good description of how the Traditions think. To put it bluntly, the meta-paradigm that the Traditions want to enforce (comparable to the way you interpret the Principles of Damian) it's nothing other than the Purple Paradigm that aligns with the Methaphysics of Magick (which doesn't necessarily means it has to be true).<br /> They believe that will makes reality, raising your arm it's not as likely to light you on fire as not because there's a will component that's not negotiable. This it's what makes the Traditions different from the DIsparate Aliance (well, among other things).<br /> Because the Purple Paradigm it's too hard to swallow even for mages (and ultimately it doesn't work as a Paradigm, as no one can &quot;have&quot; it. This it's why I use the composed word &quot;meta-paradigm&quot;. It's more a &quot;catch all&quot; for Paradigms/Practices than something that can work on itself ), the Traditions don't try teaching this to the masses just as the Technocracy doesn't try to teach the core methapisical concepts of the principles of Damian (heck they hide this concepts even from their own), but rather they strive to make the world accept more and more practices (which contributes to open the road for their utopical end goal).<br /> <br /> And now, thanks to M20, the Traditions have a way to measure their victories and defeats in the Ascencion War, by seeing how Reality Zones evolve.<br /> It's pretty much stated that in some wild places the mundane technology that you cherish as &quot;part of Reality&quot; doesn't work, and the subtlest Technomagick it's Vulgar...<i>this isn't what the Traditions want. </i><br /> The fact that, in a world where supposedly &quot;everyone knows that magic it's bullshit&quot;, people (normal people) wants to summon spirits to bless their laptops prooves that the technomagical approach works. In places where technoshamanism it's common a Reality Zone it's formed and technochamans can use magick coincidentaly. And this kind of Reality Zones are the ones that I think refflect better what the Traditions believe, in these places technology isn't going to be canceled, no need to go back to the DA.<br /> <br /> If your beliefs on what the Traditions <i>are </i>were true, they would want to create Reality Zones where only old Paradigms thrive and even mundane tech doesn't work...I don't see this as an accurate representation of what the Traditions want. In places where technoshamanism works, I would think that technology AND shamanism would work too, wouldn't you?. So, yes, I would say it does work as intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-28-2017, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T16:13:56-07:00","id":1085212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1083493-just-do-it-the-high-tech-way?p=1084752#post1084752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I say then that the Technocracy will never truly win... because that won't make for a very fun game.</div> </div> </div> </div>When did any Faction ever &quot;truly win&quot;? What does that even mean? What are the victory conditions for this contest?<br /> <br /> Did the Order of Hermes &quot;win&quot; in Medieval Europe? Did the Wu Lung &quot;win&quot; in the Middle Kingdom? Did the Union already win when they managed to sell their vision to the world they mapped into existence to the degree they already have? <br /> <br /> If Tradition magic works and the Traditions achieves its awaited Rapture of Mass Ascension (or even just &quot;Mass&quot; Ascension of those who buy what the Union's selling) did the Union win or lose? Or do they just need to crush their opposition, make sure every mage is dead or an Enlightened Science and every Reality Zone bulldozed, leveled and covered with mini-malls to win, even if they create a world so void of anything meaningful that any Ascension, Mass or otherwise, becomes effectively impossible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T14:20:54-07:00","id":1086785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1083493-just-do-it-the-high-tech-way?p=1085212#post1085212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When did any Faction ever &quot;truly win&quot;? What does that even mean? What are the victory conditions for this contest?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're taking my statement too seriously. I made it because I couldn't understand the previous bunch of posts and decided I wanted to say something too.<br /> <br /> Edit: But, for the sake of arguing a point for fun:<br /> <br /> The complete idea is: &quot;The Technocracy will never truly win in any objective sense because if they did, the game would end, and the mage setting we know would cease to be... and that would be no fun.&quot;<br /> <br /> If the Traditions somehow won and eradicated the Technocracy and the Nephandi, we could still have some amount of fun with champions of each major paradigm trying to gain dominance over the consensus... not that the writers are likely to do anything that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 05-02-2017, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T07:28:14-07:00","id":1087143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: But, for the sake of arguing a point for fun:<br /> <br /> The complete idea is: &quot;The Technocracy will never truly win in any objective sense because if they did, the game would end, and the mage setting we know would cease to be... and that would be no fun.&quot;<br /> <br /> If the Traditions somehow won and eradicated the Technocracy and the Nephandi, we could still have some amount of fun with champions of each major paradigm trying to gain dominance over the consensus... not that the writers are likely to do anything that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, but that's because you're assuming (correctly, I think) that the Traditions (or at least most traditionalists) are hypocrites and they don't really want that &quot;Rapture of Mass Ascension&quot; where paradigms and differences disappear (that they don't believe in the mutual respect Traditions preaches)...what they want it's just to regain enough power to start fighting for their own paradigms (which are totally the best way to reach mass ascencion).<br /> <br /> It's also possible that the Traditions divide in a &quot;civil war&quot; (like the Technocracy, but worse) between the &quot;champions of each major paradigm&quot;, and those members that defend a more syncretic way (like the Celestial Chorus, which has mages who defends the unity of all religions, and mages who believe in their religion and think all the others are pagans and heretics but joined the chorus for convenience)<br /> <br /> Here's one paranoid theory: In Ascencion 1\u00ba scenario (supposedly the one that it's a natural interpretation of the Lore, or so the book implies albeit it's not canon) Ascencion it's pretty much Armaggedon...when all people in the world Awakens, the Tenth Sphere it's revealed and Spheres align disolving the world and unifying it back to the First Age (or something like that). It's disolution, and unity, and it's the end of the world too.<br /> This vision (if it's true) it's what almost every sect will (unwittingly or not) cause if they *win*, unless we suppose that the beliefs of the people at the time when the Tenth Sphere it's revealed does matter somehow, or that the Consensus can prevent it's effects (which it's unlikely, as Paradox it's part of Judgement, but who knows).<br /> The Traditions push for Mass Ascencion, but so does the Technocracy (just that it's called Mass Empowerment, but it's the same phenomena). The Ahl i Batin Unity comes directly from it, and it seems that so does Nephandi vision (as they want the Tenth Sphere of Armaggedon to be revealed, which will cause the same end, or will it?). If I was a paranoid vampire I would think that every mage sect was manipulated so, while they believe in different world ends and search them with different means, will reach the same end product (but, if it's so, by whom?).<br /> But this it's just a theory, an Ascencion theory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-03-2017, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T15:32:27-07:00","id":1087949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1083493-just-do-it-the-high-tech-way?p=1087143#post1087143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, but that's because you're assuming (correctly, I think) that the Traditions (or at least most traditionalists) are hypocrites and they don't really want that &quot;Rapture of Mass Ascension&quot; where paradigms and differences disappear (that they don't believe in the mutual respect Traditions preaches)...what they want it's just to regain enough power to start fighting for their own paradigms (which are totally the best way to reach mass ascencion).<br /> <br /> It's also possible that the Traditions divide in a &quot;civil war&quot; (like the Technocracy, but worse) between the &quot;champions of each major paradigm&quot;, and those members that defend a more syncretic way (like the Celestial Chorus, which has mages who defends the unity of all religions, and mages who believe in their religion and think all the others are pagans and heretics but joined the chorus for convenience)<br /> <br /> Here's one paranoid theory: In Ascencion 1\u00ba scenario (supposedly the one that it's a natural interpretation of the Lore, or so the book implies albeit it's not canon) Ascencion it's pretty much Armaggedon...when all people in the world Awakens, the Tenth Sphere it's revealed and Spheres align disolving the world and unifying it back to the First Age (or something like that). It's disolution, and unity, and it's the end of the world too.<br /> This vision (if it's true) it's what almost every sect will (unwittingly or not) cause if they *win*, unless we suppose that the beliefs of the people at the time when the Tenth Sphere it's revealed does matter somehow, or that the Consensus can prevent it's effects (which it's unlikely, as Paradox it's part of Judgement, but who knows).<br /> The Traditions push for Mass Ascencion, but so does the Technocracy (just that it's called Mass Empowerment, but it's the same phenomena). The Ahl i Batin Unity comes directly from it, and it seems that so does Nephandi vision (as they want the Tenth Sphere of Armaggedon to be revealed, which will cause the same end, or will it?). If I was a paranoid vampire I would think that every mage sect was manipulated so, while they believe in different world ends and search them with different means, will reach the same end product (but, if it's so, by whom?).<br /> But this it's just a theory, an Ascencion theory.</div> </div> </div> </div>A rather silly theory considering the spheres are just artificial constructs used to help the users codify and make use of magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T15:58:42-07:00","id":1087965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1083493-just-do-it-the-high-tech-way?p=1087949#post1087949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A rather silly theory considering the spheres are just artificial constructs used to help the users codify and make use of magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they do represent metaphysical concepts that are quite real in the minds of those who use them and thus are also very real in the Astral Realms. Why cannot we propose that some strange primordial astral entity has been manipulating the minds of mages in an attempt to bring about ascension?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T16:19:02-07:00","id":1087974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChewyGranola</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1083493-just-do-it-the-high-tech-way#post1083493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I have been thinking about magick in relation to my work. I work at a bank, and when people come in asking for things like cash, paper statements, checks, etc, I always wonder what's keeping them from doing things the more high-tech way. This lead naturally (of course) to me thinking about the Syndicate, and then to how the Technocracy works.<br /> So I know that per canon most Technocrats don't see what they do as &quot;magic&quot; it's Enlightened Science, which is cool on it's own. But, what if the Technocracy viewed themselves as just the advanced modern magic users? Basically, why are you using dirt and trees and crystals when you can use computers and guns and stuff?<br /> I know this changes a lot, making the Technocracy maybe a little kinder and gentler, and I know a lot of people won't like that. And I know this could potentially not work with the idea of consensual reality, which has always been confusing and hard to do right for me anyways. I guess this could be a more recent development. This doesn't mean that the Pogrom had to go away, obviously, particularly since Technocrats view the Traditions as unstable and dangerous to everyone magic users.<br /> Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do remember, the Tehnocrats are such great villains because they see themselves as the good guys. all the best dramatic villains see themselves as the true hero. Which is why heroes always need a little self-doubt. Absolute certitude is a villain trait! The idea behind the Technocratcy is that they ARE WORKING for ascension, but they are working to make everybody do it in one way only. The Traditions know that people must be free to find their own paths. The Disperates Alliance is in fact closer to the Technocracy than the Traditions, they feel that they alone can define a worthy and proper Ascension.<br /> <br /> Remember, even the Dreamspeakers and the Hermetics have Techno factions. The Trads don't oppose Techno-Ascension. They oppose having Ascension defined by others and rammed down the masses throats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T08:47:21-07:00","id":1088312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1083493-just-do-it-the-high-tech-way?p=1087949#post1087949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A rather silly theory considering the spheres are just artificial constructs used to help the users codify and make use of magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>One would think so...but as with many things in Mage, contradictions abound.<br /> <br /> You know what's (one would think) bullshit: To search for the Tenth Sphere. If spheres are just an artificial construct then what's there to search for?...Unless you tell me that the Spheres are like a scientific model, that they aren't a mere methapor about what mages do but rather an explanation of an underlying reality that can be perfected (and thus, finding the Tenth wouldn't be silly, but an advancement of magick)...but then we wouldn't live in an entirely consensual reality, <i>or would we?</i>.<br /> <br /> Mage (usually) takes the &quot;scientific development&quot; as shaping the universe so it takes the form we want (that's, like, the opposite of real science), but if the Tenth Sphere it's both real and different from what everyone thought, if it's out there to be discovered...(and will KILL US ALL when it appears, or join us in divinity, who knows?) then we have no other choice but to conclude that Humans don't create everything...<br /> <br /> Some books say that Spheres are shards from The One or The Pure Ones...that they're like alternate universes as big as the Telluriam. Maybe they were there to be discovered.<br /> <br /> Or, maybe, things are as Spacecat says:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">But they do represent metaphysical concepts that are quite real in the minds of those who use them and thus are also very real in the Astral Realms. Why cannot we propose that some strange primordial astral entity has been manipulating the minds of mages in an attempt to bring about ascension?</span></span><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Very interesting theory<br /> <br /> Maybe that the Tenth was there in the universal subcoscious of the Consensus (right there next to vampires <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )...and in the consciousness of the many mages and archmages that search for it (and what mages search, they usually find)...<br /> <br /> Who knows how much power the Spheres gathered, backed by the untold power of hundreds of mages that lived and died behind them (and some of who turned Exemplars, Gods, and whatnot)...and maybe now they guide mages to Ascencion wheter they want or not.<br /> <br /> The only thing I want to nitpick it's that the Spheres aren't part of the Astral Umbra, they're part of the Deep Umbra (Shard Realms).<br /> But in the Deep Umbra it's said that the &quot;three worlds are one&quot;, so maybe the Spheres were born as powerful Epiphanies (where they were first developped or conceptualized), and then started growing in intensity (and in altitude) untill they reached the Deep.<br /> <br /> Also remember that Spheres aren't a modern invention, they were created in the court of Tothmes III, when they were called &quot;the nine cornerstones of reality&quot;. But maybe they are even older in some way, the concept of Time as a sepparate entity wasn't invented in Egipt, maybe like Helios sits at the top of all solar deities Time sits at the top or all temporal concepts (even those that don't necessarily agree with the concepts behind the Sphere, spirits pressent &quot;a thouzand of faces&quot; as per Book of Worlds).<br /> <br /> Some mages think that in the Astral Umbra there may be ideas that precede the human thinking. Foundational ideas necessary for the construction of the mind, so to speak, that would be quite powerful in the magical sense (they would be Uthra: Astral Celestines, as per the Book of Madness 1rst ed)...<br /> Maybe the Spheres were there all the time, as foundational concepts that exist, not before, but at the same time as the Consensus. (well, Kant did tought that Time was an &quot;a priori&quot; : \u201cPhenomena can be annihilated in thought, but as a universal condition, time cannot.\u201d. He wouldn't have tought the same about Forces or Matter, but then, he didn't contemplated reality as consensual <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-05-2017, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T11:09:58-07:00","id":1088389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1083493-just-do-it-the-high-tech-way?p=1087949#post1087949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A rather silly theory considering the spheres are just artificial constructs used to help the users codify and make use of magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are they? Considering Spheres are identical in Mage-the-game and Mage-the-game-setting, they are, for all intents and purposes, intrinsic to the construction of reality. Maybe they weren't always... (but even then they kinda were) During the Dark Ages the world's magic was a mosaic of similar but not congruent mini-praxes that were a fusion of Focus and Sphere, but, by the time of the creation of the Order of Reason and the Traditions, the Spheres seem to be THE accurate way of describing the way the universe actually works. Witness the fact, that, (with the possible exception of some dudes hanging out with vampires in the Shadowlands), <i>everyone </i>in the modern world uses the same framework, including people (like some Disparates) that deny that they are doing so. The Big Change seems to be that Focus was stripped out and the Spheres were revealed for what they were, the underlying structure of everything. Focus was also revealed as the way in which it was possible to utilize the Spheres.<br /> <br /> If the Spheres were just artificial constructs, then there would be someone out there who would have figured out different ways of doing similar things. (Dataweaver loves this, wanting a setting where what you said is fundamentally true and there are groups out there using the Foundation/Pillar system, those using the Arete/Sphere system and another as yet undefined system for the Technocratic Union that works on slightly different axes.) It's Focus (or the collected Foci of groups with similar magical methodologies) that are the artificial constructs. Spheres just are. Or, at least, they are an artificial construct that is a very close approximation of the way that the universe works to the point that, having come up with a way to articulate them, they effectively serve as a functional way to discuss something that ALL magic users have in common. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}